  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "生活阅览室 × 知识宇宙",
    "overview": "LifeAtlas now joins its familiar reading layout to the user-requested 3D knowledge universe under one continuous cosmic sky. The outlined LifeAtlas wordmark, desktop rail, independent topic index and native controls remain the identity anchors. 光屿工作台 (Island, default) and 对页观察室 (Observatory) retain their names and shared geometry, with cool blue and warm violet/peach night palettes respectively.\n\nThe November 2 integration supersedes the earlier white-sheet palette and isolated landscape treatments. Reading remains calm and legible on near-opaque dark surfaces; the sky provides spatial continuity through the navigation and transparent knowledge scene. Knowledge is a core destination alongside the existing daily and personal modules. Appearance changes preserve live work; scenery and knowledge examples never become authored personal history.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One locally generated cosmic sky spans the shell and transparent knowledge scene.",
      "A familiar LifeAtlas rail, flat topic index and continuous dark reading sheet.",
      "Two named night palettes with native controls and explicit written states.",
      "Chinese sans host UI, serif comparison excerpts, outlined wordmark and local Space Grotesk inside knowledge.",
      "Real perspective 3D exploration with a readable detail panel and compact module toolbar."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Textual State Rule",
        "body": "Every consequential status has a written label; color is an additional cue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Continuous Sky Rule",
        "body": "Use one body-level sky behind navigation and modules; the embedded knowledge renderer stays transparent rather than painting a second sky.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Index and Sheet Rule",
        "body": "The topic index locates; the near-opaque sheet carries reading. Use dividers and disclosures inside the sheet rather than another stack of equal-weight cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Live Task Rule",
        "body": "Changing appearance preserves live input, focus, scroll and the current view by updating the document skin attribute.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the active palette’s semantic CSS variables across all core and optional destinations.",
      "Do preserve the LifeAtlas wordmark, native control semantics, explicit saving, visible keyboard focus and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "Do keep topic lookup separate from continuous reading and secondary tools in native disclosures.",
      "Do keep the knowledge scene transparent over the shared sky and reading panels sufficiently opaque for long text.",
      "Do keep appearance and animation preferences exclusively in Settings → 外观与动态.",
      "Do distinguish fictional demonstrations and static knowledge content from real authored records."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't restore the superseded white-paper palettes, lake banner or horizontal Observatory desktop shell as current design authority.",
      "Don't add retired skins or duplicate brand/navigation chrome inside the embedded knowledge module.",
      "Don't remount the live route to change appearance.",
      "Don't put long reading text directly on the animated star field.",
      "Don't make editing, hidden-page or reduced-motion states keep animating the shared sky.",
      "Don't turn examples, scenery, counts or unimplemented analysis into personal data or capability claims."
